methods.explanation:
The logarithm has base \(5\), so write \(625=5^4\) to use the same base throughout. Let \(t=\log_5 2015\). By the definition of a logarithm, \(5^t=2015\).

All power bases are positive, so the laws of real exponents apply:
\[
\left(625^t\right)^{1/4}
=\left((5^4)^t\right)^{1/4}
=5^{4t/4}
=5^t
=2015.
\]
The fourth root is the positive root, consistent with \(2015>0\). Thus the value is \(\boxed{2015}\), choice D.
